Tool Name    : AJ Tools - Shared UI Theme
Purpose      : Suite-wide WPF resource dictionary (soft dark UI, Neon Blue primary). Used by every AJ Tools window.
Author       : Ajmal P.S.
Company      : AJ Tools
Version      : 1.4.0
Created      : 2025-12-10
Last Updated : 2026-08-05
Target       : 2020 - latest (A: 2020-2024 / B: 2025-2026 / C: 2027+ - verify newest)
Framework    : .NET Fx 4.7.2 (2020) / verify 4.8 (2021-2024) | .NET 8 (2025-2026) | 2027+ verify Autodesk SDK
Platform     : C# Revit Add-in (WPF)
Notes        : Brush KEY names are kept stable - every window binds to them. Only values are tuned to the AJ skill.
               Style = Neumorphism + Claymorphism soft UI; Neon Blue primary; orange = warning; red = danger; green = success.
Changelog    : v1.4.0 - Tick boxes, radio buttons and the toggle switch are properly templated at last.
               They were setter-only, so they drew raw Windows chrome inside an otherwise soft rounded
               Neon Blue UI - the last big visual inconsistency in the suite. Now: an 18px rounded box
               that fills accent-blue with a tick that scales in, a matching radio with a dot that pops,
               and ToggleSwitchCheckBox finally drawn as the switch its name always claimed, knob
               sliding 20px. All keep their original Setters, so nothing moves on any window. Kept as
               KEYED styles (no implicit CheckBox style) so the DataGrid tick column in Duct Standards
               is untouched - an animated tick there would replay on every scroll.
               v1.3.0 - Interaction motion. Hover, press, keyboard-focus and enable/disable states now
               animate instead of snapping, on buttons, window-control buttons, text boxes, dropdowns,
               list/dropdown items and tab headers; the dropdown arrow rotates when the list opens; a
               house ProgressBar style is added (with a busy pulse for indeterminate). NOTHING animates
               Background or Foreground - only overlay Opacity and RenderTransform inside a
               ControlTemplate - so a window that sets those from code-behind is never fought.
               v1.2.0 - Readability fix: accent-filled buttons (Primary/Modern/Success/Danger) and
               selected states (list items, combo items, tab headers) now use TextOnAccent (white)
               instead of the near-black TextOnLight, which was unreadable on the WinUI accent fills
               (#0078D4/#0F7B0F/#E81123). TextOnLight kept for genuinely bright fills only.
               v1.1.0 - Skill alignment: Segoe UI font, Neon Blue #00C8FF, softer card radius, button shadow trimmed, Consolas mono style.
License      : All Rights Reserved
Repo         : AJ-Tools
==================================================
